    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d728">

                <pb facs="0790" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/161: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul at Geneva (Gilbert)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-11T18:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1932—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. Your 139, April 11, 10 a.m. On February 5 and on February 25 the Department
                    requested certain of its offices in Japan and China to extend to the League
                    Commission and to General McCoy all
                    proper assistance. The Department is today sending further supplemental
                    instructions to the Legation at Peiping for transmission to the appropriate
                    consulates.</p>
                <p>You may so inform the Secretary-General.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
